medium.com/tinystories-4ce620e569a4\"},{\"title\":\"hyper.ai\",\"url\":\"https://hyper.ai/cn/datasets/33032\"},{\"title\":\"The Tiny Model Revolution with Ronen Eldan and Yuanzhi Li of Microsoft Research\",\"url\":\"https://cognitiverevolution.ai/the-tiny-model-revolution-with-ronen-eldan-and-yuanzhi-li-of-microsoft-research\"},{\"title\":\"Source code for oumi.datasets.pretraining.tiny_stories\",\"url\":\"https://oumi.ai/docs/en/latest/_modules/oumi/datasets/pretraining/tiny_stories.html\"},{\"title\":\"www.alphaxiv.org\",\"url\":\"https://www.alphaxiv.org/overview/2504.09184\"},{\"title\":\"🚀NEW COURSEVibe Coding AI Apps with Claude Code 🤖✨Enroll now\",\"url\":\"https://academy.dair.ai/papers/tinystories\"},{\"title\":\"Go backThe blogThis article\",\"url\":\"https://sfcompute.com/blog/tiny-narrations\"},{\"title\":\"meilu.jpshuntong.com\",\"url\":\"https://meilu.jpshuntong.com/url-68747470733a2f2f61727869762e6f7267/pdf/2305.07759.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"www.wizwand.com\",\"url\":\"https://www.wizwand.com/dataset/tinystories\"}]\n\nThe TinyStories results describe a synthetic story dataset from Microsoft Research, used mainly to train small language models.\n\n- **Origin:** Its authors describe it as a synthetic dataset of short stories written with words a typical 3 to 4-year-old would understand, generated by GPT-3.5 and GPT-4. The paper is by Ronen Eldan and Yuanzhi Li.\n- **Versions:** A newer release, TinyStoriesV2-GPT4, uses only GPT-4 generations, since the original set also includes lower-quality GPT-3.5 output.\n- **Licensing:** One library's documentation notes that the dataset is available under the CDLA-Sharing-1.0 license.\n- **Research use:** The paper's models target training and evaluating small language models (below 10 million parameters) to produce fluent and consistent narratives.\n- **Criticism:** A later SimpleStories paper from ETH Zürich and collaborators reported that 59% of TinyStories samples began with the formulaic phrase \"Once upon a time,\" which could bias models toward superficial patterns.\n- **Derivatives:** Other groups have built on it, including a scalable, synthetically curated dataset comprising 17 Indian languages and a synthetic audio dataset based on TinyStories.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "aeabafca-00bd-4a92-974e-cf3b6b19d3b3", "uuid": "46199384-4f4c-435e-afba-5dbe8f33b19f", "timestamp": "2026-11-02T16:18:12.913Z", "tool_use_result": {"query": "TinyStories", "results": [{"tool_use_id": "srvtoolu_01M9NGxBUdwzo17KPu1vr856", "content": [{"title": "TinyStories: How Small Can Language Models Be and Still Speak Coherent English?", "url": "https://arxiv.org/pdf/2305.07759"}, {"title": "hyper.ai", "url": "https://hyper.ai/en/datasets/33032"}, {"title": "www.huggingface.co", "url": "https://www.huggingface.co/datasets/roneneldan/TinyStories/blob/main/README.md?code=true"}, {"title": "huggingface.co", "url": "https://huggingface.co/datasets/roneneldan/TinyStories"}, {"title": "Multilingual TinyStories: A Synthetic Combinatorial Corpus of Indic Children's Stories for Training Small Language Models", "url": "https://arxiv.org/pdf/2603.14563"}, {"title": "TinyStories: How Small Can Language Models Be and Still Speak Coherent English?", "url": "https://deepai.org/publication/tinystories-how-small-can-language-models-be-and-still-speak-coherent-english"}, {"title": "TinyStories: How Small Can Language Models Be and Still Speak Coherent English?", "url": "https://www.microsoft.com/en-us/research/?p=973236"}, {"title": "Loading Events", "url": "https://www.math.harvard.edu/event/the-tinystories-dataset-how-small-can-language-models-be-and-still-speak-coherent-english/"}, {"title": "Loading Events", "url": "https://cmsa.fas.harvard.edu/event/nt-92023"}, {"title": "TinyStories: How Small Can Language Models Be and Still Speak Coherent\\n English?", "url": "https://liner.com/ko/re